  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0389 and it contains four tables: Student, Teacher, Course, and Student_Course_Selection. The Student table has five columns: Age, Gender, Name, Phone, and Student_ID, which is the primary key. The Teacher table has five columns: Gender, Name, Phone, Teacher_ID, and Title, where Teacher_ID is the primary key. The Course table has six columns: Class_Hours, Class_Location, Course_ID, Credits, Number_of_Students_Enrolled, and Teaching_Teacher_ID, where Course_ID is the primary key and Teaching_Teacher_ID is a foreign key referencing the Teacher table. The Student_Course_Selection table has four columns: Course_ID, Grades, Selection_Time, and Student_ID, where Student_ID and Course_ID are the primary key and foreign keys referencing the Student and Course tables, respectively. The primary key of the Student_Course_Selection table is a composite key consisting of Student_ID, Course_ID, and Selection_Time.",
  "gold_question": "The primary function of a school's academic management system is to manage Student, Teacher, Course information, as well as Student course selection status and grade records. The system includes the following functions:\n\nStudent Management: Record basic information about students, including Student Name, Gender, Age, and Phone.\n\nTeacher Management: Record basic information about teachers, including Teacher Name, Gender, Title, and Phone.\n\nCourse Management: ecord basic information about courses, including Course Credits, Class Hours, Teaching Teacher, Class Location, and Number of Students Enrolled.\n\nStudent Course Selection Management : \nRecord the course selection status of students, including Selection Time and Grades. Each student can select multiple courses, and each course can have multiple students enrolled.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0389.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0389\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teacher` (\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`teacher_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `credits` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_hours` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_students_enrolled` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `teaching_teacher_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teaching_teacher_id`) REFERENCES `teacher` (`teacher_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_course_selection` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `selection_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `grades` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `course_id`, `selection_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_course_selection_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_course_selection_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
